(a) Intent. It is the intent of this section to permit the temporary location of a mobile home in C-3 general commercial zones in remote areas of the city for security purposes only when all the provisions of this section are satisfied.
(b) Conditions for issuance of temporary permit. Upon a finding of necessity, the board of commissioners may, at its discretion, authorize the issuance of a temporary permit for location of a mobile home in a C-3 general commercial zone when the applicant shall demonstrate compliance with all of the following conditions:
(1) The proposed location is in a remote, outlying and generally undeveloped area of the city in which not more than ten percent of the surrounding parcels of property lying within 1,500 feet of the proposed location have been developed;
(2) The existence of a substantial security problem within or around an existing building housing a permitted use;
(3) The mobile home shall be clearly incidental to the permitted use;
(4) The mobile home is used solely to provide temporary quarters for security guards and security operations and equipment, and specifically not for general residential purposes;
(5) The mobile home is being used on a temporary basis to allow the owner to construct permanent facilities or to abate the security problem, and specifically not for an extended or permanent use;
(6) The mobile home shall be located in the rear of the buildings, and shall be secured in such manner as not to be visible from any adjacent public street right-of-way;
(7) All buffering and screening requirements of the C-3 zone are in place and in compliance with the zoning ordinance (appendix A to this Code);
(8) All other applicable requirements of the zoning ordinance (appendix A to this Code) are satisfied;
(9) A valid temporary permit will be obtained as provided in section 62-36.
The board of commissioners may impose conditions over and beyond the conditions specified in this subsection, as may be deemed necessary, to protect the interest of adjoining property owners and the health, safety and welfare of the public.
(c) Issuance of permit. All permits issued pursuant to this section shall be temporary and issued in compliance with section 62-36. All such permits shall be issued for a temporary period not to exceed 12 months.
(d) Conditions for permit renewal. Permits may be renewed under the following conditions, provided that the total permitted time shall not exceed five years, under any circumstances:
(1) A new application shall be filed no later than November 1 of the year in which the permit is issued;
(2) The remote, outlying and generally undeveloped character of the area in question continues to exist;
(3) The applicant can demonstrate continued compliance with all provisions of subsection (b) of this section.
(Code 1976, § 23-46.1)
